      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The offseason has already given this club a harder edge - less sentiment, more arithmetic. <strong>The loudest change is the departure of Mitch Marner, with his agent now saying he was \"never protected\" by the Maple Leafs, a flashpoint that explains why Toronto's summer has turned into a roster reset.</strong> The Leafs sit 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, but that finished record is only the backdrop to a new front office logic: trim the fat, mine the draft, and stop pretending the old core was sacred. John Chayka's hand is all over a roster that now leans on veteran additions and a prospect pool that, for once, has real believers. The next pressure point is obvious - who stays, who gets moved, and whether the club can turn cap space into a sturdier spine. <strong>Watch the trade market, because Toronto's next move may matter more than the one it just made.</strong>",
