        "body": "The offseason has the Raptors picking at the edges of a roster that still feels one move short of finished. <strong>Kyle Anderson's one-year, $3.9 million deal</strong> gives Toronto a steady hand on the wing, while the club's decision to keep Trace Jackson-Davis on a $2.4 million team option says the front office still wants inexpensive, flexible depth rather than a flashy splash. Toronto sits 3rd in the Atlantic Division, but that number is old wallpaper now; the real work is in cap management and the final roster spots. DeMar DeRozan chatter lingers as a sentimental tug, yet this team needs fit more than nostalgia. The bigger question is whether the Raptors add one more veteran or leave the last chair open for camp competition - <strong>that call will tell you how ambitious this summer really is</strong>.",
